{
  "$comment": [
    "Pinned sources for the external binaries bundled into the installer.",
    "build.rs reads this file; editing it is how you change what ships.",
    "",
    "sha256: null means 'record whatever we got, do not enforce'. Set it to a hex",
    "digest to make the build fail on mismatch. It is null by default for ffmpeg",
    "because BtbN re-publishes the n8.1-latest assets in place every few days --",
    "a hard pin there would break every build within the week. The URL is the pin;",
    "the recorded digest lands in binaries/.tools.json so drift is visible.",
    "",
    "yt-dlp tracks the nightly channel's latest/download, so a clean build picks",
    "up whatever is current rather than a pin that goes stale. See the note on",
    "the ytdlp entry for why nightly and not stable. Already-installed users are",
    "covered by the in-app updater, which writes to the app data dir and is read",
    "first (see the resolution order in binaries.rs).",
    "",
    "Deno used to be here, for the JavaScript runtime yt-dlp wants to answer",
    "YouTube's player challenge. It was 40 MB compressed and 95 MB on disk --",
    "two thirds of the installer -- and measuring it on 2026-09-02 against a 4K",
    "YouTube video showed `yt-dlp -J` returning the same 53 formats and choosing",
    "the same 1080p H.264 + m4a pair with it and without it. The only difference",
    "was a warning line. So it is not shipped: binaries.rs looks for deno, node,",
    "bun or quickjs on the machine instead and points yt-dlp at whichever it",
    "finds, and downloads work when it finds none."
  ],
  "tools": {
